{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: Implement `api_call_loss_filter` through `solve(case)`.\n\nFrom the description:\n1. For each call, subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call to get gain\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least 1)\n3. Accept a call if: parseable=True AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Return accepted_call_ids and diagnostics in original order\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\n- `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n- `normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)` (normalize by at least one prediction token)\n- `accepted = parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold` (inclusive threshold means \u003e=)\n\nThe output:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of call_ids where accepted=True, in original order\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain` for each call in original order\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, tokens=5, normalized = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=True → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, tokens=4, normalized = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=True → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, tokens=6, normalized = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=True → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, tokens=5, normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079 (approx), parseable=True → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, tokens=5, normalized = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=True → 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05 → NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, tokens=4, normalized = 0.76393214/4 = 0.19098304 (approx), parseable=True → accepted\n\nSo call4 is rejected due to normalized_gain \u003c threshold.\n\nThe candidate artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - need to figure out rounding. The schema says `normalized_gain` is a `number`. I'll use round to some decimal places. Looking at the description more carefully... it says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify the number of decimal places. I'll use round(..., 8) or just leave as float. Actually, let me just compute and return without explicit rounding or with minimal rounding.\n\nWait, \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics\" - maybe I should round to some reasonable precision. I'll use round(x, 8) to keep precision reasonable.\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        norm_tokens = max(tokens, 1)\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Now I need to format this as the required JSON response with `implementation` key containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        norm_tokens = max(tokens, 1)\\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / norm_tokens, 8)\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01uYX3d38qOXqbJK211ntSpE","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2376},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2376,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":13,"output_tokens":1327,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1061},"service_tier":"standard"}}